<title>PERU: Building firm Grana y Montero seeks Lima shr float.</title>
<headline>Building firm Grana y Montero seeks Lima shr float.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A leading Peruvian construction firm Grana y Montero has sought permission from the Lima Stock Exchange to float 44 million soles ($16.6 million) worth of common shares on the bolsa, an exchange source said Wednesday.</p>
<p>If the exchange approves the float, the operation will be the largest new issue on the bolsa this year, the source added.</p>
<p>Over the last two years, Grana y Montero has established itself as one of the top construction firms, winning important contracts to build office blocks, shopping malls and hotels.</p>
<p>((--Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
